Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 06:21:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): refresh class wall registry per allocation
 [daveey]

Problem: combined class wall consumers reused a module-captured assignee config closure after the registry changed. Why: helper imported the config reader by value at initialization; isolated tests could not expose stale selection. Read the reader per call; a sequential two-registry test reproduces first-provider leakage before the change and passes afterward.

Proof: canonical retries-disabled class controls 76 passed; combined 12-file class/pacing/B verification 277 passed, 11 failures retained, not ready to land. Correct historical dedupe seed, explicit class provider representation, destination pacing and ordinary paced receipt assertions without changing author or quota gates. Full scripts/check green. Original fleet remediation and review/deployment acceptance remains open.
